        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Metal Max is a 1991 vehicle combat role-playing video game developed by Crea-Tech and published by Data East for the Nintendo Famicom exclusively in Japan on May 24, 1991 and later re-released on the Wii Virtual Console on April 27, 2010. It is the first of the Metal Max series. Metal Max is set in a futuristic post-apocalyptic world, where the surviving humans cluster in underground villages and ruins while \"monster hunters\" fight the monsters and outlaws outside.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
